# 6 Automated Quantitative Evaluation

GPT-2 (Radford et al., 2019) is widely used in mechanistic interpretability research. We use model sizes ranging from S (124M) to XL (1558M) (See Table 16 in Appendix B for details). Token space $S_{\mathrm{GPT - 2}}$ contains 50,257 tokens encoded using the byte-pair encoding (BPE) algorithm (Sennrich et al., 2016). We map 31K of GPT-2's tokens directly to 19K words $\in$ Wikipedia-V40K's $V_{\mathrm{Wiki}}$ . No further processing is required, as we recover a large portion of $V_{\mathrm{Wiki}}$ .

